      "title": "Collision of two trains in Egypt kills at least four",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/egypt-two-trains-deadly-collision",
      "description": "<p>President orders prompt investigation after one train derails in collision in al-Ayyat about 30 miles from Cairo</p><p>At least four people were killed and almost 90 others were injured when two trains collided on Sunday south of Cairo, authorities have said.</p><p>The crash occurred in al-Ayyat district in Giza province, about 30 miles (5okm) south of the capital, when a train travelling to the south-western Fayoum province crashed into the rear of a train heading to the southern province of Aswan, according to the transport ministry. It said one of the trains had derailed.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/08/egypt-two-trains-deadly-collision\">Continue reading...</a>",
